/S /H3
/P 113 0 R
/T (The qilin is the gentlest creature in the Chinese bestiary: it walks without bending a blade of grass, eats no living thing, and breathes fire only in self-defense. It appears as an omen when a sage is born and vanishes when one dies. Confucius, tradition says, was born when a qilin appeared at his mother's house and died the year one was killed in a hunt. He wept.)
